## Optional audio-engine dependencies

These are optional features of the Rust engine. `decode` enables Symphonia in
the Tauri shell; `native-output` enables cpal and is not selected by a shell.

| Component | Used for | License |
| --- | --- | --- |
| cpal 0.15 | Optional native audio output in the Rust engine | Apache-2.0 OR MIT |
| symphonia 0.5 | Decoding MP3, AAC/M4A, FLAC, Ogg/Vorbis, WAV, AIFF and ADPCM | MPL-2.0 |

MPL-2.0 is file-level copyleft: modifications to Symphonia's own files must be
published under MPL-2.0, while OpenDeck's files can remain MIT. We do not
modify Symphonia; if that changes, the modified files will be called out here.

## Session tempo transport (opendeck-link/1)

`src/main/link.ts` implements an original session tempo/beat/phase transport
published under OpenDeck's MIT licence. It is **not** Ableton Link and does not
interoperate with Ableton Live: it uses its own multicast group
(`239.255.77.88:29876`) and its own message format (`opendeck-link/1`), both
documented in `docs/mobile/ADR-D34.md`.

No Ableton Link code, crate, package, model or asset is included, vendored,
linked or downloaded. Ableton's reference implementation is dual-licensed
GPLv2+/proprietary, and every implementation of its wire protocol found during
this run is GPL; the licence decision and its consequences are recorded in
`docs/mobile/ADR-D34.md`.

"Ableton" and "Link" are trademarks of Ableton AG, used here only to state what
this software is not compatible with. No endorsement or affiliation is implied.

